+++ b/docs/V166_DATABASE_GUARD_ATTESTATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# MASTER7 v166 database guard attestation
+
+Release: `17.0.0-selfbuilt.166-database-guard-attestation`
+
+## Purpose
+
+Migration markers prove that a guard was installed once. They do not prove
+that the physical PostgreSQL trigger still exists, remains enabled, or still
+invokes the intended function. v166 adds a fail-closed attestation on every
+portal database initialization.
+
+## Startup contract
+
+The portal verifies nine critical triggers covering provider-wallet contract
+immutability and both acceptance ledgers. Each trigger must match the frozen
+contract for:
+
+- public table and trigger name;
+- enabled state `O`;
+- public trigger-function name;
+- PostgreSQL trigger type;
+- exact `UPDATE OF` columns where applicable.
+
+The check runs after migrations 0120 and 0122 and before directory seeding,
+inside the existing transaction and migration advisory lock. Missing,
+disabled, duplicate, wrong-table, rebound, malformed, or wrongly scoped
+triggers abort startup and roll back all work in that transaction. The startup
+path never recreates or enables a drifted trigger automatically.
+
+The PostgreSQL readiness gate imports this same frozen contract so startup and
+external evidence cannot drift onto different trigger lists.
+
+## Schema and operational scope
+
+This release adds no table or migration. Backup schema remains
+`0122-acceptance-ledger-integrity`, with its existing schema hash and 76-table
+coverage. v166 does not change payment credentials, provider endpoints,
+wallet balances, payment or game submission flags, DNS, or service plans.
+
+## Verification
+
+Unit tests cover the exact nine-trigger contract, ordering before seed,
+idempotent second startup, rollback, and rejection of missing, disabled,
+duplicate, wrong-table, wrong-function, wrong-schema, wrong-type, and wrong
+column-binding evidence. The isolated PostgreSQL 18 test additionally damages
+live trigger metadata after the migration marker exists, proves that restart
+fails closed, restores the trigger explicitly, and proves that restart passes.
+
+All provider and money paths remain closed during validation.
